# =============================================================================
# Kingdom Mission Network (.org) - Environment Configuration
# =============================================================================

# App Configuration
VITE_APP_NAME=Kingdom Mission Network
VITE_APP_URL=https://kingdommissionnetwork.org

# Feature Flags
VITE_ENABLE_LIVE_STREAMING=true
VITE_ENABLE_DONATIONS=true

# API Backend (leave empty for Cloudflare Pages same-origin deployment)
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Supabase Configuration
# Frontend (Public)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Backend Cloudflare Worker / Server Environment Variables:
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
# JWT_SECRET=your-secure-random-jwt-secret

# Google OAuth (Optional: Google Cloud Console > APIs & Services > Credentials)
# Authorized JavaScript origin: https://kingdommissionnetwork.org
# Authorized redirect URI: https://your-project.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Email Delivery (Resend - https://resend.com)
# Verify domain: kingdommissionnetwork.org
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxx
# RESEND_FROM_EMAIL="Kingdom Mission Network <giving@kingdommissionnetwork.org>"
# RESEND_EVENTS_EMAIL="Kingdom Mission Network <events@kingdommissionnetwork.org>"

# Paystack (M-Pesa, Mobile Money & Cards - https://dashboard.paystack.com)
# Webhook URL: https://kingdommissionnetwork.org/api/subscriptions/webhook
# Callback URL: https://kingdommissionnetwork.org/subscribe?paystack_callback=1
VITE_PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_live_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Backend env: PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# PayPal (International Checkout - https://developer.paypal.com)
# PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=your-paypal-client-id
# PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=your-paypal-client-secret

# Wise API (Live Currency Exchange Rates - https://wise.com)
# Backend env: WISE_API_TOKEN=your-wise-read-token

# Sentry (Observability & Error Tracking - https://sentry.io)
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://xxx@xxx.ingest.sentry.io/xxx
# SENTRY_DSN=https://xxx@xxx.ingest.sentry.io/xxx

# Billing engine (renewal dunning cron + OTP claim hardening)
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# CRON_SECRET=your-long-random-cron-secret
# Cron schedule (every 6h): POST /api/subscriptions/billing/retry-due with header x-cron-secret
# Renewal nudges: GET /api/subscriptions/billing/due?days=2 with header x-cron-secret
# KCB Buni STK: KCB_BUNI_CONSUMER_KEY / KCB_BUNI_CONSUMER_SECRET / KCB_BUNI_ENV=sandbox|production
#
# Provider webhook guard (recommended in production):
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# MPESA_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your-long-random-webhook-secret
# When set, Daraja C2B / KCB IPN / KCB STK-callback must send header x-webhook-secret.
# When unset (local dev / tests) callbacks preserve legacy ack behaviour.
#
# Production hardening:
# ENVIRONMENT=production  (blocks credentialed http://localhost:* CORS origins)
# FRONTEND_URL=https://kingdommissionsnetwork.org  (extra allowed CORS origin)
#
# M-Pesa STK Push availability (frontend + backend must agree):
# - Keep "false" while KCB Buni is in sandbox. STK UI hides; /mpesa/stkpush returns 503.
# - Set "true" AND KCB_BUNI_ENV=production only after KCB go-live approval.
# VITE_ENABLE_STK_PUSH=false
#
# Paybill ground truth (PRODUCTION PATH while STK is disabled):
# Pasted SMS codes NEVER activate on format checks. Activation requires a
# provider-confirmed receipt in mpesa_paybill_receipts. Register BOTH:
#  1. Daraja C2B Confirmation URL on paybill 522522 (Register-URL API, one-time):
#       https://kingdommissionsnetwork.org/api/subscriptions/mpesa/c2b-confirmation
#     Validation URL (optional, permissive ack):
#       https://kingdommissionsnetwork.org/api/subscriptions/mpesa/c2b-validation
#  2. KCB Buni IPN target for collection-account credits:
#       https://kingdommissionsnetwork.org/api/subscriptions/mpesa/kcb-ipn
# Until (1) or (2) is registered, Paybill codes stay `awaiting_receipt` and
# must be approved in the admin reconcile queue after checking the statement.
# OUR_PAYBILL=522522 / OUR_ACCOUNT=1335674365 are pinned in backend/src/lib/paybill.ts
#
# ── SANDBOX MODE walkthrough (no live paybill touched) ─────────────────────
# The code paths are IDENTICAL in sandbox and production; only the shortcode,
# credentials, and flags differ. In sandbox you register URLs on Daraja's TEST
# shortcode (e.g. 600984), never on 522522 (production registration is a
# one-time go-live step with the 522522 owner / KCB).
#
# A. Daraja sandbox (https://developer.safaricom.co.ke):
#   1. Create app → consumer key/secret. Set MPESA_CONSUMER_KEY/SECRET (backend).
#   2. Expose callbacks publicly for local dev: ngrok http <api-port>
#      (Daraja must reach your ConfirmationURL; free ngrok URLs change on restart.)
#   3. Register URLs on the TEST shortcode (one call, sandbox):
#      curl -X POST https://sandbox.safaricom.co.ke/mpesa/c2b/v1/registerurl \
#        -H "Authorization: Bearer <OAUTH_TOKEN>" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#        -d '{"ShortCode":"600984","ResponseType":"Completed",
#              "ConfirmationURL":"https://<you>/api/subscriptions/mpesa/c2b-confirmation",
#              "ValidationURL":"https://<you>/api/subscriptions/mpesa/c2b-validation"}'
#   4. Fire a test payment (sandbox C2B Simulate; BillRefNumber MUST be 1335674365
#      for redemption matching, amount = the plan price under test):
#      curl -X POST https://sandbox.safaricom.co.ke/mpesa/c2b/v1/simulate \
#        -H "Authorization: Bearer <OAUTH_TOKEN>" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#        -d '{"ShortCode":"600984","CommandID":"CustomerPayBillOnline","Amount":3000,
#              "Msisdn":"254708374149","BillRefNumber":"1335674365"}'
#      → Safaricom POSTs the confirmation to your URL → receipt row created.
#   5. Redeem: paste the simulated TransID in the app Paybill form → 201 active.
#      Or redeem first (202 pending claim) then simulate → auto-fulfilled.
#
# B. Shortcut without Daraja (double-locked, NEVER in production):
#      ALLOW_SANDBOX_TOOLS=true  (and KCB_BUNI_ENV != "production")
#      POST /api/subscriptions/mpesa/simulate-receipt
#        {"transId":"TK78AB12CD","amount":3000,"billRef":"1335674365"}
#      → writes a sandbox receipt + auto-fulfills any open claim for that code.
#
# C. KCB Buni UAT (https://sandbox.buni.kcbgroup.com): subscribe app to
#    MpesaExpressAPIService, keep KCB_BUNI_ENV=sandbox (STK stays 503-locked;
#    UAT STK does not reach real handsets). Production flip checklist:
#    KCB_BUNI_ENV=production + VITE_ENABLE_STK_PUSH=true + ALLOW_SANDBOX_TOOLS
#    unset + provider URLs registered on the live shortcode/account.

